# Feature Module Structure

Each `screen-{feature}` module follows this layout:
```
screen-{feature}/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/ijs/{feature}/
├── data/
│   ├── datasource/{Feature}RemoteDataSource.kt
│   ├── mapper/{Feature}Mapper.kt
│   ├── model/{Feature}Dto.kt, {Feature}Request.kt
│   └── repository/{Feature}RepositoryImpl.kt
├── domain/
│   ├── entity/{Feature}.kt
│   ├── repository/{Feature}Repository.kt (interface)
│   └── usecase/{Feature}UseCases.kt
└── presentation/
    ├── {Feature}Contract.kt
    ├── {Feature}ViewModel.kt
    ├── {Feature}Screen.kt
    └── {Feature}FeatureFacade.kt
```

## FeatureFacade — public entry point
```kotlin
object {Feature}FeatureFacade {
    @Composable
    fun {Feature}ListEntry(viewModel: ..., onNavigateBack: ..., onNavigateTo...: ...) {
        {Feature}Screen(viewModel, onNavigateBack, onNavigateTo...)
    }
}
```
- Facade is the **only public API** — screens/VMs are `internal` where possible
- `sharedUI` navigation calls Facade entries, never screen composables directly
- Each screen gets its own Facade entry function

## Role-based access
- Owner/GM see all financial data (trip_price, P&L, revenue)
- Manager sees operational data only (no prices, no P&L)
- Supervisor is view-only (can only update trip status)
